abstract: >-
  This project aims to develop a benchmark dataset for phase-field fracture mechanics, focusing on fracture propagation of 
  multiple initial defects on a 2D hyperelastic domain with a spherical inclusion under quasi-static cyclic loading. 
  The numerical model captures the non-linear stress-strain behavior of the hyperelastic material. The dataset 
  consists of simulations for 1000 distinct loading conditions applied as boundary constraints, providing 
  detailed insights into crack initiation and propagation patterns. This will be a valuable resource for 
  validating computational methods and advancing data-driven approaches in fracture mechanics.

